Description: pvr: do not inline the stream return of deferred secondaries
 A secondary command buffer recorded with RENDER_PASS_CONTINUE ends its
 control stream with VDMCTRL_STREAM_RETURN (pvr_arch_cmd_buffer_end_sub_cmd(),
 secondary_cont). Without SIMULTANEOUS_USE the primary reaches that stream
 through a VDMCTRL_STREAM_LINK with with_return set, so the return goes back
 to the primary. With SIMULTANEOUS_USE the stream is deferred and
 pvr_arch_csb_copy() copies it into the primary stream itself, including the
 return. The primary stream is not entered through a link with return, so the
 return is not matched by a call, and everything the primary emits after the
 copy (further secondaries, the end of the render) follows it.
 .
 Drop the trailing VDMCTRL_STREAM_RETURN when copying a deferred stream, so
 the copied commands continue in the primary stream like commands recorded in
 the primary.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
